From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 14:45:03 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: bcm4377: restore private PCI windows
 before J713 resume

Shared radio PERST resets private BAR windows that generic PCI saved
state does not cover. Restore the windows and subsystem control in
resume_noirq, before interrupts or UNQUIESCE access the retained device.
Without this, Wi-Fi returns after sleep but Bluetooth HCI commands time
out. Restoring the windows permits Read Local Version to complete.

Coordinate QUIESCE and recovery work with the managed host transaction,
leaving other controllers on their existing path. Cover config failures
and retained-path skips with a fault-injection fixture.

Signed-off-by: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
[niteria: bcm4377-resume-tests' mocks now have the radio sleep hooks]
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Bartosz Nitka <niteria@gmail.com>
[dylan: hand-ported from aurora-silicon/linux d810b1f6874d (PR #1384) to
 the J604's unmanaged radio port: only the resume_noirq window restore is
 taken, gated on pm_resume_via_firmware() alone; the managed radio-sleep
 coordination (apple_radio_sleep_*), the J713-only gating, the fixture
 and the panic on a failed restore (an error return here) are left out;
 see the upstream commit for the full change]
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm4377.c | 40 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 39 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm4377.c b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm4377.c
index 46f0f933bf..25967e3e96 100644
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm4377.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm4377.c
@@ -21,6 +21,7 @@
 #include <linux/pci.h>
 #include <linux/printk.h>
 #include <linux/property.h>
+#include <linux/suspend.h>
 #include <linux/workqueue.h>
 
 #include <linux/unaligned.h>
@@ -3195,7 +3196,44 @@ static int bcm4377_resume(struct device *dev)
 	return ret;
 }
 
-static DEFINE_SIMPLE_DEV_PM_OPS(bcm4377_ops, bcm4377_suspend, bcm4377_resume);
+/*
+ * A sleep that powered the radio off (on the J604 the APCIe block goes down
+ * with ANS for a T8132 deep sleep) resets the private BAR windows, which
+ * PCI's saved config state does not cover. Restore them before the IRQ
+ * handler or UNQUIESCE reaches the controller through them. Suspend-to-idle
+ * keeps power and does not resume via firmware, so it skips this.
+ */
+static int bcm4377_resume_noirq(struct device *dev)
+{
+	struct bcm4377_data *bcm4377 = pci_get_drvdata(to_pci_dev(dev));
+	u32 before = 0, after = 0;
+	int ret;
+
+	if (!pm_resume_via_firmware())
+		return 0;
+
+	ret = pci_read_config_dword(bcm4377->pdev, BCM4377_PCIECFG_BAR0_WINDOW1, &before);
+	if (!ret)
+		ret = bcm4377_init_cfg(bcm4377);
+	if (!ret)
+		ret = pci_read_config_dword(bcm4377->pdev, BCM4377_PCIECFG_BAR0_WINDOW1, &after);
+	if (ret > 0)
+		ret = pcibios_err_to_errno(ret);
+	if (!ret && after != bcm4377->hw->bar0_window1)
+		ret = -EIO;
+	if (ret) {
+		dev_err(dev, "private PCI windows not restored after a power loss: %d\n", ret);
+		return ret;
+	}
+	dev_info(dev, "private PCI windows restored after a power loss (%#x -> %#x)\n",
+		 before, after);
+	return 0;
+}
+
+static const struct dev_pm_ops bcm4377_ops = {
+	SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS(bcm4377_suspend, bcm4377_resume)
+	.resume_noirq = bcm4377_resume_noirq,
+};
 
 static const struct dmi_system_id bcm4377_dmi_board_table[] = {
 	{
